WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.947
Use this decision guide when designing modular SQL.

00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:05.667
Choose a CTE for statement-local stages.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:08.537
Choose a standard view for stable shared live logic.

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:12.387
Use a simple updatable view only when write behavior is intentional.

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:16.152
Use views with proper privileges for controlled interfaces.

00:00:16.152 --> 00:00:24.262
Choose a materialized view when storing a reusable result is worth the freshness tradeoff.

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:28.527
Keep highly changeable report thresholds outside stable shared objects.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:31.852
Choose the smallest reusable object that matches the need.

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:36.187
A CTE is local to one query, a view centralizes live logic, and a materialized view persists a snapshot.

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:43.312
Promote logic into shared objects when it is stable, reused, and worth governing as part of the analytical

00:00:43.312 --> 00:00:44.827
architecture.
